{"created": "2026-08-24T21:19:50.327141+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-24T21:19:50.579196+00:00", "id": 22087163, "conceptrecid": "22087162", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22087162", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "metadata": {"title": "An Explicit Windowed Sparsity Bound for Divergent 3x+1 Orbits, with Logarithmic-Floor Exclusion beyond the Harmonic Barrier", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "publication_date": "2026-08-24", "description": "<p>&nbsp;Garcia and Tal proved in 1999 that every infinite orbit of the 3x+1 map has Banach density zero. We give a short self-contained proof of an explicit quantitative form: for every infinite aperiodic orbit, the number of orbit points in any window [a, a+X) is at most C X^b log(2X) uniformly in a, for every b &gt; 0.96538..., with the exponent equal to Rozier's critical ones-ratio times log2(3). Three consequences follow for the Syracuse map with valuation drift g_n: every divergent orbit has summable reciprocals; no divergent orbit satisfies g_n &lt;= B log2(n) + O(1) eventually for any B &lt;= 1; and an occupation bound extends the exclusion to every B &lt; 1.03585... This passes the threshold 8/9 recently proved by De Jesus and shown there to be terminal for congruence-packing, and it settles the graded harmonic-thinness requirement of his Open Problem 12.8 in a stronger form than requested. No claim is made on cycles, on the Effective Occupation Conjecture, or on the Collatz conjecture itself.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Curry, Michael John", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher"}], "keywords": ["Collatz conjecture", "3x+1 problem", "Syracuse map", "Banach density", "divergent orbits"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22087162"}}]}}, "title": "An Explicit Windowed Sparsity Bound for Divergent 3x+1 Orbits, with Logarithmic-Floor Exclusion beyond the Harmonic Barrier", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22087163", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22087163?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22087163", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087162", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22087162", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22087162", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22087162", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22087163:occupation_note_clean.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22087163/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/2